From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:12:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Module groups: --structure-disabled leaves out a named group

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: a configuration that shows its modules in groups, with a
heading (a custom module) and a break for each, cannot be shortened
from the command line: --structure-disabled takes module types, and
leaving out "cpu" and "display" leaves the "Hardware" heading and its
break behind. A preferences editor that offers "show: system,
hardware, memory, network" would need its own copy of the preset for
every combination.
Solution: a module object may have "group": "<name>".
--structure-disabled leaves out every module whose group it names, as
it leaves out a type. The key is accepted by every module (with
"type" and "condition") and described in the JSON schema and help.
Scope: common/impl/jsonconfig.c, the four modules that check their
own keys (break, logo, separator, users), doc/json_schema.json,
doc/help.json. All platforms; a configuration without "group" is read
as before.
Upstream-Status: could be proposed upstream; not submitted.
Verification: guest runs with the aros-logo and aros-compact presets
and --structure-disabled hardware:network (see the evidence for
2.70.0-r3).
Removal: if upstream adds a way to disable a set of modules.
